{"content":[{"c":["SCURVY"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Term used three times in the Bible (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.20","r":"Lev.21.20","rawR":"Lev.21.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.20","value":"Lev.21.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 21:20"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.22.22","r":"Lev.22.22","rawR":"Lev.22.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.22.22","value":"Lev.22.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:22"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.28.27","r":"Deut.28.27","rawR":"Deut.28.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.28.27","value":"Deut.28.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 28:27"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). In none of the instances does it refer to the modern disease by the same name, which results from severe vitamin C deficiency. In the Leviticus passages, “scurvy” is found in the sequence “scurvy or scabbed.” This phrase is translated “oozing sores or scabs on his skin” in the ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Disease_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Disease_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Disease_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Disease"},"; ",{"href":"?item=MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Medicine and Medical Practice"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Scurvy","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Lv 21:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.21.20","rawQueryValue":"Lev.21.20","sourceRefExact":"Lev.21.20"},{"anchorText":"22:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.22.22","r